# Vauxhall Cresta PC saloon, 1965-1972.
#
# The PC: the last Cresta, the coke-bottle body with the fastback roofline,
# sold as the Cresta and, in its V8 form, as the Viscount. There was no Velox
# PC; the Cresta stood alone. The saloon is modelled; the estate and the
# Viscount are not separately represented.
# https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vauxhall_Cresta
#
# Dimensions: saloon 4,710 x 1,770 x 1,410 mm, wheelbase 2,730 mm. The estate
# is 4,750 mm long and 1,500 mm high; the Viscount saloon is 4,790 mm.
#
# Shape reference: image 1 is a true level side profile; the flank is traced
# from it.
#
# Colours: grade (d); no period Vauxhall colour list was found. Black, Grey,
# Blue and Green are plain period names. Weights 12, 10, 9, 8, total 39,
# provisional.
#
# Speed 155 km/h. Comfort 65/428, on the line 330 + 1.5 x 65. Classes 1,2,3.
# Dates: intro October 1965; retires staggered 1979-1982 as a road tail.
#
# Metres master: citycars/4.5/vauxhall-cresta-pc.blend. Interchange:
# citycars/4.5/vauxhall-cresta-pc.dae. References:
# citycars/references/vauxhall-cresta-pc/ (gitignored).
#
# Accepted deviations: the Cresta De Luxe quad-lamp saloon only. No Velox,
# Viscount vinyl roof, estate roof line or auxiliary spotlights are
# represented.


obj=citycar
name=VauxhallCrestaPC(Black)
copyright=JamesPetts

DistributionWeight=12
intro_year=1965
intro_month=10
retire_year=1982
retire_month=6
speed=155
length=3
class=1,2,3
maximum_comfortable_journey_minutes=65
maximum_tolerable_journey_minutes=428

